  "Number": 10,
  "Question": "The number of positive integers \\(k\\) for which the equation \\[ kx-12=3k \\] has an integer solution for \\(x\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(6\\)",
    "E": "\\(7\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Rearranging the equation gives\n\\[k(x-3)=12.\\]\nSince \\(k>0\\), the solution \\(x=3+12/k\\) is an integer exactly when \\(k\\) is a positive divisor of \\(12\\).\n\nThe positive factor pairs of \\(12\\) are\n\\[(1,12),\\qquad (2,6),\\qquad (3,4).\\]\nThese are exhaustive: each factor pair must contain a number at most \\(3\\), because \\(4\\cdot4>12\\). The pairs give the six distinct values \\(k=1,2,3,4,6,12\\), and each produces an integer \\(x\\). Therefore the answer is \\(\\boxed{6}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
